<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The English original.

  Every string a driver reads should live here rather than in Kotlin, and the
  reason is not tidiness: Saarthi's platform supports twenty-six Indian
  languages, the web app is fully localised, and registration already asks a
  driver which language they read. The Android app spoke English regardless —
  so a fleet owner could run Saarthi in Maithili and the driver, the person
  least likely to read English and the one using it every day, could not.

  Extraction is under way rather than finished. The screens below are done; the
  cockpit, scanner, approval and profile screens still hold their strings in
  Kotlin and are listed in the handover. A half-translated screen is worse than
  an untranslated one, so `Language.available` offers only the languages whose
  files are actually complete.
-->
